---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Calquna: everyday calculators, worked out properly"
  description="Free calculators for dates, health, money and words. Each one shows its working. No sign-up, and nothing you type leaves your browser."
>
  <h1>Everyday calculators, worked out properly.</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Calquna is a small set of calculators for the questions people actually ask: how old am I in
    days, how many nights until the baby is due, what does this salary pay per hour. Each tool
    shows the formula it used and a worked example, so you can check the answer instead of
    trusting it.
  </p>
  <p>
    <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/age-calculator/" style="display:inline-block;text-decoration:none;">Start with the age calculator</a>
  </p>

  <h2 id="dates">Dates and time</h2>
  <table class="catalogue">
    <thead>
      <tr><th scope="col">Tool</th><th scope="col">What it answers</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><a href="/age-calculator/">Age calculator</a></td>
        <td>Your exact age in years, months and days, plus the same span counted in weeks, days and hours.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><a href="/days-between-dates/">Days between dates</a></td>
        <td>The number of days between any two dates, with a working-days count if you leave out weekends.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2 id="words">Words</h2>
  <table class="catalogue">
    <thead>
      <tr><th scope="col">Tool</th><th scope="col">What it answers</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><a href="/word-counter/">Word counter</a></td>
        <td>Words, characters, sentences and reading time for any text you paste in. The text never leaves the page.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2 id="health">Health</h2>
  <table class="catalogue">
    <thead>
      <tr><th scope="col">Tool</th><th scope="col">What it answers</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><a href="/bmi-calculator/">BMI calculator</a></td>
        <td>Your body mass index, the band it falls in, and the healthy weight range for your height. It says plainly what BMI cannot tell you.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><a href="/due-date-calculator/">Due date calculator</a></td>
        <td>An estimated due date from the first day of your last period, how far along you are, and when each trimester turns.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><a href="/sleep-calculator/">Sleep calculator</a></td>
        <td>Bedtimes counted back from your alarm in full 90 minute sleep cycles, so you wake at the end of one.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2 id="money">Money</h2>
  <table class="catalogue">
    <thead>
      <tr><th scope="col">Tool</th><th scope="col">What it answers</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><a href="/compound-interest-calculator/">Compound interest calculator</a></td>
        <td>What a lump sum and monthly deposits grow to, year by year, with what you put in and what the interest added kept separate.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><a href="/salary-to-hourly-calculator/">Salary to hourly calculator</a></td>
        <td>What a yearly salary pays per hour, week and month, worked out on the hours you actually work. Converts back the other way too.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><a href="/percentage-calculator/">Percentage calculator</a></td>
        <td>The three percentage sums on one page: percent of a number, what percent one number is of another, and percentage change.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>School and study</h2>
  <table class="catalogue">
    <thead>
      <tr><th scope="col">Tool</th><th scope="col">What it answers</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><a href="/gpa-calculator/">GPA calculator</a></td>
        <td>Your grade point average on the 4.0 scale, weighted by credit hours the way colleges count it.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Utilities</h2>
  <table class="catalogue">
    <thead>
      <tr><th scope="col">Tool</th><th scope="col">What it answers</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><a href="/password-generator/">Password generator</a></td>
        <td>Strong random passwords and passphrases, made on the page with proper randomness. Nothing is sent anywhere.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><a href="/qr-code-generator/">QR code generator</a></td>
        <td>A QR code for a web address, your Wi-Fi, or a contact card, drawn locally and downloaded as a picture. No tracking inside the code.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Creator tools</h2>
  <table class="catalogue">
    <thead>
      <tr><th scope="col">Tool</th><th scope="col">What it answers</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><a href="/youtube-money-calculator/">YouTube money calculator</a></td>
        <td>What your monthly views are worth in ad revenue, by channel kind, given as an honest range.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><a href="/tiktok-money-calculator/">TikTok money calculator</a></td>
        <td>Creator Rewards per thousand qualified views, what a brand post might pay, and your engagement rate.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><a href="/instagram-unfollowers-checker/">Instagram unfollowers checker</a></td>
        <td>Who does not follow you back, from your own Instagram data export, read inside your browser. No login, no password, no upload.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="well">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0;">How to read an answer here</h2>
    <p>
      Every calculator on Calquna prints three things under the result: the formula, one example
      worked through by hand, and the date the page was last checked. If an answer here ever
      disagrees with your own arithmetic, write to us through the contact page and we will fix
      the page, not argue.
    </p>
    <p class="meta">This page was last checked on 13 November 2026.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
